            <ArticleTitle>Fluorinated trimethyllysine as a 19F NMR probe for trimethyllysine hydroxylase catalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1350-1354</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6ob02683d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trimethyllysine hydroxylase (TMLH) catalyses C-3 hydroxylation of Nε-trimethyllysine in the first step of carnitine biosynthesis in humans. Studies on TMLH have been hampered by the lack of established chemical methods. We report that an Nε-trimethyllysine analogue that contains the fluoromethyl group can be used as a 1H and 19F NMR probe for studies on TMLH catalysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
